HUMOR TECHNIQUES — Use these deliberately:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. SUBVERT EXPECTATIONS
   Setup creates one expectation → punchline goes somewhere completely different
   Example: "Finally saved up for a nice Martin guitar" → "Time to play nothing but G C D"

2. SPECIFICITY OVER GENERALITY
   Vague = not funny. Hyper-specific = hilarious.
   BAD:  "When the musician plays too loud"
   GOOD: "When the flatpicker starts soloing over your banjo break and makes direct eye contact the whole time"

3. ESCALATION / ABSURDIST SPIRAL
   Start normal → get progressively more unhinged
   Level 1: Practicing scales
   Level 2: Practicing at 2am
   Level 3: Your neighbors now know all of Foggy Mountain Breakdown by heart
   Level 4: The ghost of Earl Scruggs appears and tells you to keep it down

4. RELATABLE PAIN POINTS
   Things that are painfully true but nobody says out loud
   "Telling people you play banjo and watching them try to hide their reaction"

5. CALLBACK / INSIDE JOKES
   Reference things only real fans would know
   Deep cuts > obvious references (Bill Monroe's death stare > "I like bluegrass")

6. CONTRAST / JUXTAPOSITION
   Put two incompatible things together
   "Corporate wants you to find the difference: [1952 Bill Monroe] [2024 Billy Strings]"

7. DEADPAN ABSURDISM
   State something completely ridiculous as if it's normal
   "Normal Tuesday night for a mandolin player (crying in 2/4 time)"

8. META-HUMOR
   Make fun of the format itself, meme culture, or the act of making memes

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
WHAT NOT TO DO:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
- Don't explain the joke in the meme text (if you have to explain it, it's not funny)
- Don't use "Nobody: / Absolutely nobody:" format (overused, lazy)
- Don't make generic music jokes that could apply to any genre
- Don't punch down or be mean-spirited (punch up or sideways)
- Don't use puns unless they're genuinely clever
- Don't be safe — take actual creative risks

